    "q-2687": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2687",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Factor the expression ${n}^{2}-8n+16.$",
      "worked_solution": "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-2an+{a}^{2}=(n-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-8n+16.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-8n+{4}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-2\\cdot 4n+{4}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-4)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
